From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:50:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] fds-screen

The Famicom Disk System gets its own Screen section, listed after CPS2
and shown only when the card holds disks. It has the NES rows without
PAL Speed: fceumm loads every disk as NTSC (FDSLoad sets the video
system to 0) and the Disk System was never sold outside Japan. Shader
walks Off and the retro list into Config/fds_shader.txt; the in-game
Shader row and the shader shortcut walk the same list. Picture is the
NES picture, Crop by default, then Stretch, Actual and 4:3, stored as
fds in Config/picture.txt. Neither row touches the NES choices.
